Amadeus for Codex
=================

Third-party and upstream attribution
------------------------------------

This project is a reimplementation for Codex Desktop. Parts of its design and
some tool logic are derived from:

  1. amadeus-for-dsh — https://github.com/yyxcnasd/amadeus-for-dsh
     MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 yyxcnasd
     Reused: Edge TTS emotion/prosody profiles, word-boundary timing approach,
     Live2D lip-sync and idle-animation approach, emotion-to-expression map,
     asset download source.

  2. Amadeus2026 — https://github.com/Lx1228/Amadeus2026
     MIT License, Copyright (c) Lx1228
     Design reference only (architecture and interaction design). No source
     code is copied from this project.

  3. lingshu (灵枢) — https://github.com/FuRongJun-1999/lingshu
     MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 FuRongJun-1999
     Ported (with simplification): the contradiction-detection mechanism in
     src/core/contradiction.mjs — near-duplicate gating plus polarity / number /
     antonym diffing, including the non-negating-word exemption list. The test
     scenarios in tests/memory-supersede.test.mjs are adapted from that
     project's bench/repro (bench_correction.py, bench_supersede.py).

  4. HAST-SEC — https://github.com/sola1039/HAST-SEC
     Non-commercial study/research licence. NO CODE IS USED OR COPIED from this
     project. Only two UX ideas were adopted: a single `npm run check`
     pre-flight command, and a one-line command for importing your own
     character file.

Retired web implementation
--------------------------

The obsolete web panel, pixi.js, pixi-live2d-display, WebView2 SDK and their
browser verification tools have been removed from the current source tree.
Earlier Git revisions retain the original third-party license notices beside
their corresponding code. The active panel uses native Qt/OpenGL and Live2D.

Release asset
-------------

  - Amadeus application icon — scripts/Amadeus.ico
    Converted into a multi-resolution Windows icon from the Amadeus logo
    supplied by the project maintainer from an earlier Amadeus application;
    the maintainer confirmed permission to redistribute it. This statement
    does not grant rights to other character artwork or voice samples.
  - Opening animation and call-screen logo — native/sprite_logo.png and
    native/amadeus-logo.png. Copied from the Amadeus installation supplied by
    the project maintainer. These assets are separate from the MIT code license.
  - Runtime media — assets/media (catalogued in assets/media/catalog.json).
    The maintainer supplied five authored Live2D runtime variants, fourteen
    background music tracks, eight scene images and a bgm13 incoming-call
    music file, and explicitly requested their inclusion in v1.0.0.
    The models were prepared using See-through and PSD2Live. Their outputs,
    the character artwork, scene images and music are separate from the MIT
    source-code license; rights remain with their respective rights holders.
    Editing projects, model-authoring tools and cloned voice samples are not
    included. See docs/随附素材与使用.md for the exact distribution scope.

